{"summary":"The grey-headed gull (Chroicocephalus cirrocephalus), also known as the grey-hooded gull, is a small gull which breeds patchily in South America and Africa south of the Sahara. It is not truly migratory, but is more widespread in winter. This species has occurred as a rare vagrant to North America, Italy and Spain. As is the case with many gulls, it has traditionally been placed in the genus Larus.","wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chroicocephalus cirrocephalus","cells":[[-17.0,11.6,1],[-18.3,16.5,1],[-19.0,17.2,2],[-17.6,19.3,1],[-19.0,15.8,1],[-15.6,25.7,1],[-19.0,27.1,1],[-19.0,24.3,1],[-21.0,32.0,1],[-15.6,35.5,2],[-16.3,28.5,1],[-20.3,22.9,1],[-18.3,23.6,1],[-16.3,34.8,2],[-15.6,27.8,1],[-15.6,29.2,1],[-19.0,23.6,1],[-21.6,32.0,1],[-15.6,28.5,1],[-20.3,26.4,2],[-19.6,22.9,1],[-17.6,24.3,2],[-17.0,27.8,1],[-17.0,28.5,1],[-16.3,29.2,1],[-21.6,35.5,2],[-18.3,24.3,1],[-15.6,27.1,2],[-17.6,25.0,3],[-17.6,25.7,2],[-17.6,30.6,2],[-32.2,22.1,1],[-23.6,15.8,1],[-31.1,17.2,1],[-29.2,16.5,1],[-34.0,19.3,1],[-34.0,21.4,1],[-34.6,21.4,1],[-32.8,18.6,1],[-26.7,15.1,2],[-31.7,17.9,1],[-34.6,20.7,2],[-34.6,18.6,2],[-33.4,17.9,2],[-22.3,14.4,2],[-32.2,18.6,2],[-34.6,20.0,2],[-22.9,14.4,3],[-33.4,18.6,2],[-34.6,19.3,3],[-34.0,22.1,3],[-34.0,18.6,3],[-32.8,17.9,2],[-29.2,31.3,1],[-32.8,25.0,1],[-32.8,28.5,1],[-24.2,25.7,1],[-32.2,22.1,1],[-25.5,32.0,1],[-28.0,27.1,1],[-24.8,26.4,1],[-23.6,31.3,1],[-28.6,25.0,1],[-24.2,32.0,1],[-28.6,26.4,1],[-29.8,30.6,1],[-32.8,27.8,1],[-24.8,33.4,1],[-29.2,30.6,1],[-31.1,30.6,1],[-25.5,31.3,1],[-24.8,31.3,1],[-25.5,33.4,1],[-30.4,30.6,1],[-22.3,31.3,1],[-23.6,35.5,1],[-25.5,28.5,2],[-27.4,32.0,1],[-29.2,32.0,2],[-33.4,25.0,2],[-26.7,27.1,1],[-30.4,25.7,1],[-25.5,30.6,1],[-25.5,32.7,1],[-27.4,25.7,1],[-26.1,29.2,2],[-26.7,29.2,2],[-25.5,27.1,2],[-26.7,28.5,2],[-24.8,32.0,1],[-24.8,28.5,2],[-31.1,25.0,1],[-24.8,29.2,2],[-26.1,27.8,2],[-33.4,26.4,1],[-29.8,31.3,2],[-26.1,32.7,2],[-26.7,27.8,1],[-34.0,25.0,2],[-28.6,32.0,3],[-29.2,